      "body": "Removes three namespace aliases:\n\n| Removed | Use instead (the same function) |\n| --- | --- |\n| `cudnn.torch.block_sparse_attention_forward` | `cudnn.block_sparse_attention_forward` or `cudnn.BSA.block_sparse_attention_forward` |\n| `cudnn.torch.block_sparse_attention_backward` | `cudnn.block_sparse_attention_backward` or `cudnn.BSA.block_sparse_attention_backward` |\n| `cudnn.torch.block_sparse_attention_fp8_forward` | `cudnn.block_sparse_attention_fp8_forward` or `cudnn.BSA.block_sparse_attention_fp8_forward` |\n\nThey were added in #1111 and shipped in 1.30.0 and 1.31.0. No caller was found: TransformerEngine, FlashInfer, Megatron-LM and JAX (heads of 2026-10-12/13) do not reference them, and GitHub code search finds no other user. This follows #1597, which removed the `cudnn.jax`/`cudnn.torch` grouped SwiGLU aliases.\n\n`cudnn.torch` keeps the SDPA provider (`calls`, `install`, `served_plan_names`).\n\nChanges:\n- `cudnn.torch`: drop the names from `__all__` and `__getattr__`.\n- `test_BSA_jax_parity.py::test_torch_runtime_without_jax` calls the top-level functions and asserts the `cudnn.torch` names are gone.\n- `bsa.md`: the example imports from `cudnn`.\n- API index: the three names are removed.\n\nTesting, on an SM100 GPU with CUDA JAX 0.11.2:\n- `test/python/block_sparse_attention/cutedsl/test_BSA_jax_parity.py`, `test/python/block_sparse_attention/jax/test_bsa_jax.py` and `test/python/api_index`, all markers: 44 passed, 2 skipped. One skip needs two visible GPUs; the other needs `CUDNN_API_INDEX_PACKAGE_ROOT`.\n- The API index scanner matches the edited baseline, apart from the environment artifact below.\n- pre-commit passes.\n\nEnvironment note: `develop`'s C++ does not build against the shared backend build on this machine, so the package under test was this branch's Python with a compiled module from an earlier build. That module lacks the optional `gnn_agg_*` symbols (9 names in the index scan). This PR changes no C++.\n\n@coderabbitai ignore\n",
